.TH ZVM-USE 1 "October 2026" "ZVM v0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-use \- select the active Zig version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm use
.RB [ --global ]
.RI [ version ]
.br
.B zvm use --sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select an installed Zig version and update the executables exposed through
ZVM's
.I bin
directory.
The version may be exact, shorthand, or an alias; see
.BR zvm (1).
If it is not installed, ZVM offers to install it before selecting it.
.PP
In a shell set up with
.BR zvm-env (1)
(that is, while
.B ZVM_MULTISHELL_PATH
names a per-shell link), only that shell's link is changed and
.I bin
is left alone.
.PP
When no version is supplied, ZVM attempts to read
.B .minimum_zig_version
from
.I build.zig.zon
in the current project.
.PP
An installation may also be a link under the ZVM base directory to a local
Zig build containing a
.B zig
or
.B zig.exe
executable.
Its directory name can be used as the version argument.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --sync
Read a
.B //! zvm-lock:
directive from
.I build.zig
in the current directory and select its version.
Selection follows the current shell's scope.
When combined with
.BR --sync ,
.B --global
is ignored.
.TP
.BR -g ", " --global
Change the global default
.RI ( ~/.zvm/bin )
even in a shell set up with
.BR zvm-env (1).
That shell keeps its own version until it runs
.B zvm use
again.
Without a per-shell link,
.B --global
behaves exactly like plain
.BR "zvm use" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm use 0.14.1
zvm use stable
zvm use --sync
zvm use --global 0.15.2
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-env (1),
.BR zvm-install (1),
.BR zvm-list (1),
.BR zvm-alias (1)
